  "name": "FIBRINOGEN ACTIVITY",
  "code": "1550",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Fibrinogen is a <strong data-start=\"100\" data-end=\"116\">glycoprotein</strong> produced by the liver that is essential for blood clot formation. It is converted by thrombin into fibrin during the clotting process. The <strong data-start=\"256\" data-end=\"284\">Fibrinogen Activity test</strong> measures the functional ability of fibrinogen to form clots.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Fibrinogen Activity Level</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;400 mg/dL</strong></td>\n<td><strong>High</strong> &mdash; May indicate inflammation, tissue injury, infection, trauma, cancer, or pregnancy. Also an acute-phase reactant.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>200&ndash;400 mg/dL</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Normal</strong> &mdash; Functional fibrinogen level is adequate for clot formation.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>100&ndash;200 mg/dL</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Borderline Low</strong> &mdash; May suggest mild coagulopathy; monitor if clinically indicated.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&lt;100 mg/dL</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Low</strong> &mdash; Suggests impaired clotting, which may occur in:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>- Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>- Liver disease</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>- Fibrinolysis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>- Congenital hypofibrinogenemia/afibrinogenemia</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1726\" data-end=\"1753\"><strong data-start=\"1730\" data-end=\"1753\">Clinical Relevance:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1755\" data-end=\"2104\">\n<li data-start=\"1755\" data-end=\"1903\">\n<p data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"1903\"><strong data-start=\"1757\" data-end=\"1778\">Increased levels:</strong><br data-start=\"1778\" data-end=\"1781\">Seen in <strong data-start=\"1791\" data-end=\"1813\">acute inflammation</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1815\" data-end=\"1829\">infections</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1831\" data-end=\"1845\">malignancy</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1847\" data-end=\"1857\">trauma</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1859\" data-end=\"1872\">pregnancy</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"1878\" data-end=\"1900\">nephrotic syndrome</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1905\" data-end=\"2104\">\n<p data-start=\"1907\" data-end=\"2104\"><strong data-start=\"1907\" data-end=\"1928\">Decreased levels:</strong><br data-start=\"1928\" data-end=\"1931\">May result in <strong data-start=\"1947\" data-end=\"1985\">delayed or impaired clot formation</strong>, increasing the risk of bleeding. Common in <strong data-start=\"2030\" data-end=\"2037\">DIC</strong>, <strong data-start=\"2039\" data-end=\"2065\">advanced liver disease</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"2070\" data-end=\"2103\">genetic fibrinogen deficiency</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"2111\" data-end=\"2144\"><strong data-start=\"2115\" data-end=\"2144\">Important Considerations:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2146\" data-end=\"2342\">\n<li data-start=\"2146\" data-end=\"2249\">\n<p data-start=\"2148\" data-end=\"2249\">This test differs from <strong data-start=\"2171\" data-end=\"2198\">fibrinogen antigen test</strong>, which measures fibrinogen quantity, not function.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2250\" data-end=\"2342\">\n<p data-start=\"2252\" data-end=\"2342\">Should be interpreted alongside <strong data-start=\"2284\" data-end=\"2310\">PT, aPTT, D-dimer, FDP</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"2316\" data-end=\"2341\">clinical presentation</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
